cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "grokking-tda: a framework for studying grokking through topological data analysis"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Chishti
    given-names: Omar
    affiliation: "Department of Computing, Imperial College London"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/omar-chishti/grokking-tda"
abstract: >-
  A research framework for measuring topological signatures of grokking. It trains small
  models on modular arithmetic, records each training trajectory as an immutable artifact,
  and computes persistent homology over training alongside Fourier, weight-norm and local
  intrinsic dimension baselines, so that the question of what topology adds over cheaper
  diagnostics is built into the design rather than argued after the fact.
keywords:
  - grokking
  - topological data analysis
  - persistent homology
  - deep learning
  - modular arithmetic
